Peter Snelling (snelling@bnr.ca) wrote:
: It's always annoyed me that some characters have "intrisic" abilities
: which aren't really intrinsics which anyone else could gain.
: 
: For example:
: 
: - Priests have the ability to determine blessed/uncusred/cursed status
: - Priests and Ninja's have better kicking ability
: - Priests get a shorter prayer time out
: - Archeologists can identify any gems
: - (no others spring to mind)

Knights identify weapons (and/or armor, not sure which)
Wizard know all of one type of magic item, perhaps its wands.
Priests can turn the undead.  This can be used like a prayer, and has the
same time out rules as one as well.

Wizards get natural teleport control before anyone else (15th level if
I'm not mistaken).

: I think that ANY character class should be able to gain ANY intrinsic,
: even those pseudo intrinsics listed above.

I dis-agree.  Some things are implicit in being a particular class.
Priests get a shorter prayer time out because they have learned about
prayer. 

